Chapter: Lwm2mCoaps
  cites Net chapter Lwm2mClient
  cites Net chapter DtlsEndpoint

 LwM2M over coaps://: the registration client's CoAP datagrams carried as
 DTLS application data. LwM2M is the reason the transport had to be
 secured at all -- a device that can be told to reboot, or whose lifetime
 and server URI can be rewritten, is a device whose management channel is
 the whole attack surface (RFC 9147 is the transport; OMA LwM2M 1.1
 requires DTLS for the `coaps` binding).

 This is the same shape as `CoapsEndpoint` and deliberately a separate
 chapter rather than a generalisation of it: the two wrap DIFFERENT
 machines. `CoapsEndpoint` carries a request/response interaction with
 retransmission and NSTART 1; this carries a registration lifecycle whose
 states are registered, updated and gone. What they share is the carrier
 -- seal each datagram at send, slice the peer's accumulated plaintext
 from a read offset -- and if a third machine ever needs it, that carrier
 is what to lift out, not either endpoint.

 ONE LWM2M MESSAGE PER RECORD, as for CoAP: the datagram boundary is the
 message boundary, and the sealing preserves it.

 We say:

Section: Types

  Lwm2mCoapsEp = record {
    xl-client : Lwm2mClient,
    xl-dtls : DtlsEp,
    xl-read : Integer
  }

  Lwm2mCoapsStep = record {
    xls-ep : Lwm2mCoapsEp,
    xls-out : List (List Integer)
  }

Section: Construction

  lwm2m-coaps-new : Lwm2mClient, DtlsEp -> Lwm2mCoapsEp
  lwm2m-coaps-new (c) (d) = Lwm2mCoapsEp { xl-client = c, xl-dtls = d, xl-read = 0 }

  lwm2m-coaps-idle : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-idle (ep) = Lwm2mCoapsStep { xls-ep = ep, xls-out = [] }

Section: Sending

  lwm2m-coaps-seal-all : Lwm2mCoapsEp, List (List Integer), Integer, List (List Integer) -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-seal-all (ep) (dgrams) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length dgrams then Lwm2mCoapsStep { xls-ep = ep, xls-out = acc }
    else let st = dtls-ep-send-app (ep.xl-dtls) (list-at dgrams i)
    in lwm2m-coaps-seal-all (__record-set ep "xl-dtls" (st.es-ep)) dgrams (i + 1) (acc & (st.es-out))

  lwm2m-coaps-register : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-register (ep) =
    let ls = lwm2m-client-register (ep.xl-client)
    in lwm2m-coaps-seal-all (__record-set ep "xl-client" (ls.ls-client)) (ls.ls-out) 0 []

  lwm2m-coaps-update : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-update (ep) =
    let ls = lwm2m-client-update (ep.xl-client)
    in lwm2m-coaps-seal-all (__record-set ep "xl-client" (ls.ls-client)) (ls.ls-out) 0 []

  lwm2m-coaps-deregister : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-deregister (ep) =
    let ls = lwm2m-client-deregister (ep.xl-client)
    in lwm2m-coaps-seal-all (__record-set ep "xl-client" (ls.ls-client)) (ls.ls-out) 0 []

  lwm2m-coaps-tick : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-tick (ep) =
    let ls = lwm2m-client-tick (ep.xl-client)
    in lwm2m-coaps-seal-all (__record-set ep "xl-client" (ls.ls-client)) (ls.ls-out) 0 []

Section: Receiving

 A record that fails to open leaves the peer's plaintext buffer untouched,
 so the slice is empty and the registration machine is never reached --
 which is what a forged or tampered management command must do, and it is
 the whole reason this composition exists.

  lwm2m-coaps-recv : Lwm2mCoapsEp, List Integer -> Lwm2mCoapsStep
  lwm2m-coaps-recv (ep) (rec) =
    let st = dtls-ep-recv-app (ep.xl-dtls) rec
    in let buf = dtls-ep-app-in (st.es-ep)
    in let n = list-length buf
    in if n <= ep.xl-read then lwm2m-coaps-idle (__record-set ep "xl-dtls" (st.es-ep))
    else let msg = lwm2m-coaps-slice buf (ep.xl-read) n []
    in let ls = lwm2m-client-recv (ep.xl-client) msg
    in let ep2 = __record-set (__record-set (__record-set ep "xl-dtls" (st.es-ep)) "xl-client" (ls.ls-client)) "xl-read" n
    in lwm2m-coaps-seal-all ep2 (ls.ls-out) 0 []

  lwm2m-coaps-slice : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  lwm2m-coaps-slice (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else lwm2m-coaps-slice bs (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at bs i))

Section: Accessors

  lwm2m-coaps-registered : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Boolean
  lwm2m-coaps-registered (ep) = lwm2m-client-registered (ep.xl-client)

  lwm2m-coaps-executions : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Integer
  lwm2m-coaps-executions (ep) = lwm2m-client-executions (ep.xl-client)

 A server that answered is not a server we know, and on this protocol the
 distinction is the difference between a reboot we asked for and one an
 attacker asked for. The peer's identity is the DTLS endpoint's verdict.

  lwm2m-coaps-authenticated : Lwm2mCoapsEp -> Boolean
  lwm2m-coaps-authenticated (ep) = dtls-ep-authenticated (ep.xl-dtls)
